  "note": "deltaE is CIE76 in L*a*b* (about 2 is just noticeable, 10 is clear at a glance, 20 and more are different colours); contrast is the WCAG luminance ratio (1 to 21). The deuteranopia and protanopia columns repeat deltaE after the Machado 2009 simulation. Terrain colours are measured on the untoned rasters. A variant's hide is the mean of its Raptor's and T-Rex's hide pixels (hue 195 to 250, saturation at least 0.2, value at least 0.4), navy the same hues below value 0.4, amber hue 8 to 45 with saturation at least 0.75, cream hue 30 to 58 with saturation 0.1 to 0.45 and value at least 0.85. The Caveman's fur is measured on rows 46 to 64 and his skin and paint on rows 22 to 44. Steadiness compares a pattern variant with the plain sprite it was edited from; a pixel counts as changed beyond an RGB distance of 48.",
